By AM–GM, $x_{n+1}\ge y_{n+1}$ for all $n$ (and $x_1>y_1$). Then
- $x_{n+1}=\frac{x_n+y_n}2\le x_n$: $(x_n)$ is decreasing;
- $y_{n+1}=\sqrt{x_ny_n}\ge y_n$: $(y_n)$ is increasing;
- $y_1\le y_n\le x_n\le x_1$: both are bounded.

So both converge, say to $L$ and $M$. Passing to the limit in $x_{n+1}=\frac{x_n+y_n}2$ gives $L=\frac{L+M}2$, so $L=M$.

